==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|available|ity}}; attested since the early 1800s.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əˌveɪ.ləˈbɪl.ɪ.ti/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-availability.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/əˌveɪ.ləˈbɪl.ɪ.ti/|[əˌveɪ.ləˈbɪl.ɪ.ɾi]|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|+}}

# {{lb|en|chiefly|uncountable}} The quality of being [[available]].
#: {{ux|en|What is your '''availability''' this week?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1960|month=September|author=P. Ransome-Wallis|title=Modern motive power of the German Federal Railway: Part One|journal=Trains Illustrated|page=553|text=With an axleload of 16¾ tons they have a fairly wide <small>[route]</small> '''availability''' and they have been designed for ease of maintenance.}}
# {{lb|en|countable}} That which is available.
#: {{ux|en|We have several '''availabilities'''.}}

